Been playing for years, 219 games on NAO my local games before I found
NAO would probably double that number.

At first I played random characters like most everyone. Then I moved
on to Orc-Barbarians, mostly because they can eat anything and I kept
having problems with dying to fainting.

Finally I moved on to Dwarven Valkyries because they..well they are
what everyone else uses to ascend the first time.

Game was pretty generic.

Found and did Sokoban got the BoH
Found dwarf town.
I usually prefer to find magic resistance before doing mines end but
ended up getting impatient and it went fine.
Then did Fort Ludios got REALLY lucky with a Black Dragon because I
did not have reflection. Lost some key armor but got it back
elsewhere. Did get Intrinsic Regeneration out of the deal though.
Then did Medusa, pretty easy. I have gotten to her and defeated her
multiple times before without issue.
Found the castle level and proceeded to use alchemy and enchant armor
scrolls to totally over prepare. -36 AC all the important resistances.
Also did the Class Quest in this time period.
Did Castle and with switching back between oilskin for the eels and
magic cloak for everything else I accidentally forgot to switch one of
the times and lost the oilskin, some more key armor (namely speed
boots) but managed to clear out the castle regardless. With the wand I
was able to replace my lost armor and proceed.

This was the first time I had ever even made it to the castle. So
despite my stupidity with the armor switching I was pretty psyched at
this point.

Then I found out the game gets kind of boring after the castle.
Absoloutely none of the demon bosses were even remotely a challenge. I
was pretty darn paranoid about Eeels, kraken and mind flayers so I
killed them all at a distance. I took this time to seriously over-
prepare. More alchemy, writing armor enchant scrolls. Etc. etc. I did
accidentally lose my protection at some point and was never quite sure
why. But it was easy to re-earn as I had lots of priests in the upper
dungeons. I repeatedly used the tactic of letting my pets kill them to
get my money back.

I cut easy pathways on all 48 levels between the vibrating square and
the level 1 upstairs. Set all my important ascension tools in an
icebox at level 1. Killed Rodney, did the invocation, got the amulet,
rushed upstairs, using a collection of 60+ blessed teleport scrolls
for as many levels as I could. Used a forgotten spell to confuse
myself and gold detect scrolls to find the portals on all the planes.
The only plane that really gave me a hard time was the air plane,
Those elementals are annoying and numerous. But I got past them. On
Water I used my blessed genocide to get rid of ; immediately.

The Astral was not really that bad either, despite not realizing I had
forgotten my helm of opposite alignment in the dungeons and as a
result ending up going to all 3 altars till I found mine.

Ascended.

The rest is history. Now on to Crawl. ;-)

